ToolsEnabled was founded and created by Joshua Pinckard.
This standalone implementation was prepared from a review of the ToolsEnabled
engine's public catalogue, with a smaller, explicit MCP capability surface.
It does not modify or bundle any other ToolsEnabled product.

The opt-in Windows desktop adapter derives from the MIT-licensed ToolsEnabled
desktop app, revision 092a87516d9a4005bb4b3340eecfb7869d715c94, shell/accessibility-desktop.cjs
and shell/accessibility-desktop.ps1. Mouse input derives from
shell/screen-control-native.ps1. Modifications add window-only capture,
left-half positioning, and capture-bound single-action pointer input.
The original app's host approval/session UI is not included or impersonated.

ToolsEnabled source provenance and the decision taken for every legacy tool
are recorded in the source repository, not in this package. LICENSE carries
the MIT grant.

Browser integration uses Microsoft's Playwright and Playwright MCP, licensed
under Apache-2.0. The Model Context Protocol TypeScript SDK and Ajv use MIT.
These packages and their dependency licenses are installed by npm; their
copyright and license notices remain in their respective distributions.

A release archive carries those packages with it, unmodified, in
app/node_modules. Its file THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt is generated from
npm-shrinkwrap.json and lists every bundled package with the licence it
declares and the full text of the licence and notice files it ships.
No web browser is part of a release archive.
